  {
    "id": "layer:factorization-algorithms",
    "name": "Factorization Algorithms",
    "description": "Core prime factorization algorithm implementations. Includes Classical trial division, Lehman's algorithm (threaded), the Elliptic Curve Method (ECM with steps 0-2 using Montgomery curves and Lucas chains), and the Self-Initializing Quadratic Sieve (SIQS with polynomial generation, sieving, partial relation matching, Block Lanczos linear algebra over GF(2), and SQUFOF). SIQS classes form an inheritance chain: FirstPolynomial -> Sieve, Maths -> Matrix -> Relation -> Siqs. Depends on Big Integers and ECM Support layers.",
